Dear Professor Dean Adams and  Professor Michael Collyer,

Thank you for the additional remarks. I agree with you and feel it is difficult to imagine the trait evolution when phylogenetic corrections are made.
The following question related to this thread is general question about the phylogenetic comparison method rather than the geomorph, so please answer them if you would.
I known that you are very busy but, any feedback you may have, would be very much appreciated.

In the paper you wrote (Adams and Collyer, 2019: Annu. Rev. Ecol. Evol. Syst. 50: 405-425), you agree with Polly et.al <http://et.al>. 2013 and discuss the difficulty of interpreting the results of phylogenetic PCA. Polly et al. 2013 also discusses the dangers of phylogenetic corrections in modularity and integration studies at the end of the "Discussion" section. What are your thoughts on this issue?

Sincerely,
Naoto Toyoda

